From 3dada20146cda20da6caa8cb8e962b3c151c6d88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:00:53 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/31] kcm_access: area list with one Form page per area;
 screen-reader D-Bus calls cached and async

Page type: List (main) + Form (each area), docs/page-design.md. kaccessrc/kwinrc keys, KWin effect calls, kded
screenreader calls and defaults are unchanged. NOT BUILT YET (owner stopped heavy work); checked statically only.

Moved / renamed:
- The sidebar + Loader (AbstractKCM) is now a short list (ScrollViewKCM) grouped Seeing / Typing / Pointing / Alerts
  (HIG-001/005/006: most used first, grouped by what the user is trying to do). Each row shows a one-line description
  and its current state (On/Off, Full screen zoom...), and keeps the "changed from default" dot. A row opens its area
  with kcm.push(). Area names are the old sidebar names.
- Every page is KCM.SimpleKCM + Kirigami.FormLayout (was Kirigami.Form/FormGroup/FormEntry), sections as
  Kirigami.FormData.isSection, first section untitled, dependent options indented and disabled not hidden (Zoom keeps
  hiding the options of the mode that is not selected).
- "Enable" checkboxes now say what they do ("Use sticky keys", "Ignore repeated presses of the same key",
  "Click when pointer remains still", "Correct colors", "Allow inverting screen colors", "Play a sound when the bell
  rings", "Signal the bell on the screen") (HIG-057). Spin box labels sentence case ("Delay time:"). Help text moved
  from the intro paragraph to a small label (Color Blindness) and ContextualHelpButtons next to the checkbox.
- Text Size: the two buttons got labels and the hint under each; hints wrap at gridUnit*16.
- Screen Reader page uses kcm.screenReaderInstalled (computed once) instead of a second PATH search; Orca feedback
  shown as a small label under the button.
- Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_access.tsv (outer repo); old wording added to the page aliases in ia/layout.json.
  All 54 inventory rows kept, `inventory_check.py --kcm kcm_access --strict`: 0 lost.
- Not changed (needs the manager's OK): the embedded KShortcutsDialog buttons that duplicate kcm_keys
  (ia/duplicates.md); Invert/Color Blindness stay here although kcm_kwin_effects lists the same effects.

Speed (cause found in code, kcms/access/kcmaccess.cpp):
- load() made a blocking session-bus call to kded6 /modules/screenreader before the first frame (kded may have to start
  the module). Worse, isSaveNeeded() and screenReaderIsDefaults() each made another blocking call on EVERY evaluation,
  and screenReaderIsDefaults() is bound by the Screen Reader sidebar row and called through isDefaults() by the shell.
  Now: load() sends the two calls (enabled, enabledByDefault) asynchronously with QDBusPendingCallWatcher and caches the
  results; isSaveNeeded()/screenReaderIsDefaults() compare cached values; save() updates the cached saved value.
- Before, all 11 areas' QML was reachable from one 45x25 gridUnit page and the first area (Zoom & Magnifier, 339 lines,
  ObjectModel + 2 Repeaters) was always instantiated; now the first frame is a 11-row list and an area is created only
  when opened.
- save() still makes synchronous KWin calls (only on Apply, not on open).
- After numbers: pending, manager will measure (was ~5.9 s ready at 0.5 CPU under load).

Not built yet; API shapes used were grepped in src/master (kirigami ListSectionHeader.label, KCM ScrollViewKCM.view,
KQuickConfigModule::push, ContextualHelpButton.toolTipText, SettingStateBinding as before).

